  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only multiprofile models dominate image-only models, and scvi_n200 with avgpool is the strongest configuration so far (0.650 accuracy / 0.628 F1). Transformer aggregation was worse than avgpool for PCA, but its effect with the stronger scvi representation is still unknown. config_006 tests only aggregation while keeping the best RNA encoder and multiprofile setting, cleanly isolating whether transformer aggregation can improve the top RNA representation. This is the best next use of budget because it reduces key uncertainty about aggregation before adding multimodal fusion or testing weaker image-based directions."
